  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The RPS and MSIV system actuation was caused by the Mode Switch 05A-S1 failing to enact the logic required to bypass the Group 1 isolation on Main Steam Line Low Pressure (PCIS) and the MSIV Closure RPS Trip when taken to the Start & Hot STBY position. The most likely cause of failure of proper switch contacts make-up was that the mode switch was operated slowly to perform detailed inspection of switch components and gearing per scheduled preventative maintenance activity, resulting in all contacts not making up properly.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "Mode switch contacts failed to make up properly during slow manual operation for inspection, compounded by lack of procedural validation",
    "provisional": true
  },
